{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "P51164", "secondaryAccessions": ["B1B0N8"], "uniProtkbId": "ATP4B_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1996-10-01", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-06-10", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "1996-10-01", "entryVersion": 185, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta"}}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "Gastric H(+)/K(+) ATPase subunit beta"}}, {"fullName": {"value": "Proton pump beta chain"}}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000312", "source": "HGNC", "id": "HGNC:820"}], "value": "ATP4B"}}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P18597"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P19156"}], "value": "The beta subunit of the gastric H(+)/K(+) ATPase pump which transports H(+) ions in exchange for K(+) ions across the apical membrane of parietal cells. Plays a structural and regulatory role in the assembly and membrane targeting of a functionally active pump (By similarity). Within a transport cycle, the transfer of a H(+) ion across the membrane is coupled to ATP hydrolysis and is associated with a transient phosphorylation of the alpha subunit that shifts the pump conformation from inward-facing (E1) to outward-facing state (E2). Interacts with the phosphorylation domain of the alpha subunit and functions as a ratchet, stabilizing the lumenal-open E2 conformation and preventing the reverse reaction of the transport cycle (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P18434"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P18597"}], "value": "The ATPase pump is composed of two subunits: alpha (catalytic) and beta (regulatory). Interacts with alpha subunit ATP12A; this interaction is required for the formation of a functionally active pump and targeting at the plasma membrane (By similarity). Interacts (via N-terminus) with alpha subunit ATP4A (via the P-domain) (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "INTERACTION", "interactions": [{"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P51164", "intActId": "EBI-3904463"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "O95273", "geneName": "CCNDBP1", "intActId": "EBI-748961"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P51164", "intActId": "EBI-3904463"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "O15529", "geneName": "GPR42", "intActId": "EBI-18076404"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P51164", "intActId": "EBI-3904463"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q9NQZ6", "geneName": "ZC4H2", "intActId": "EBI-747993"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}]}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "note": {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P20648"}], "value": "Localized in the apical canalicular membrane of parietal cells"}]}, "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P20648"}], "value": "Apical cell membrane", "id": "SL-0015"}, "topology": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}], "value": "Single-pass type II membrane protein", "id": "SL-9906"}}, {"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P18597"}], "value": "Cell membrane", "id"